NAME
     patch - apply a diff

SYNOPSIS
     patch [-p N] [-R] [-i FILE] [-o FILE] [-b]

DESCRIPTION
     patch reads a unified or context diff and changes the files it
     names. What it cannot place it writes to a .rej file beside the
     original and says so.

OPTIONS
     -p N      strip N leading directories from the names in the diff
     -R        apply the diff backwards
     -i FILE   read the diff from FILE rather than standard input
     -o FILE   write the result to FILE rather than in place
     -b        keep the original as .orig

SEE ALSO
     diff(1)
